      <span style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">LEGAL COMPLIANCE</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When relocating to or from Dewas, ensuring the safety of your two-wheeler requires meticulous documentation. Professional packers and movers in Dewas adhere to strict regulatory standards to facilitate smooth bike transportation.</p>
<p>Providing accurate paperwork not only speeds up the loading process but also serves as your primary legal protection against potential transit damages or disputes. The following documents are essential for a seamless and compliant move.</p>

<p>First and foremost, you must provide a self-attested photocopy of your vehicle’s Registration Certificate (RC). This document establishes the legal ownership of the bike and is mandatory for any inter-state or intra-state transport authorization.</p>
<p>Alongside the RC, a current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate is required. While this may seem irrelevant for a bike being transported on a carrier, it validates that your vehicle is in a roadworthy condition and compliant with local environmental regulations, which some logistics partners verify before accepting the load for insurance purposes.</p>

<p>Furthermore, a valid insurance certificate for the vehicle itself must be presented. This distinct from the transit insurance discussed below; it ensures that your personal vehicle insurance is active and unexpired. Finally, the most critical operational document is the IBA-approved consignment bilty.</p>
<p>The Indian Banks’ Association (IBA) approved bilty acts as the official bill of lading. It details the sender, receiver, description of goods, and the agreed-upon freight charges. Without this standardized document, the transport company cannot legally release the bike to the recipient, and you lack a formal contract for the service rendered.</p>

<p>Beyond standard documentation, financial protection is paramount. We strongly highlight the necessity of 100% declared-value marine transit insurance. Unlike standard cargo cover, which may only compensate for a fraction of the loss, marine transit insurance covers the full market value of your bike as declared in the bilty.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">This coverage includes protection against accidental damage, theft, fire, and natural disasters during the journey.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Given the vulnerability of two-wheelers to scratches, dents, or total loss during transit, opting for this comprehensive coverage eliminates financial risk.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Ensure that the declared value on the bilty matches the current market value of your bike to avoid under-insurance claims.</span></li></ul>

